{"id":161353241058516,"type":"artist","name":"Old Time Relijun","artist":null,"year":1995,"weight":12,"info":{"tags":["experimental","noise rock","Lo-Fi","indie rock","indie"],"country":"US","begin":"1995","kind":"Group","similar":["Thinking Fellers Union Local 282","Deerhoof","Royal Trux","Black Eyes","Half Japanese","Oxbow","Liars","The Dead C","Scratch Acid","This Heat"],"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/cc7edcf0b1eb5024089a7fedce0e83b1/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"Old Time Relijun is a three-piece ensemble formed in Olympia, Washington in 1995. With frequently rotating drummers (the current drummer is Germaine Baca, but past drummers have included Phil Elvrum a.k.a the Microphones), the main stalwarts are Arrington de Dionyso (vocals, guitar) and Aaron Hartman (stand-up bass). Dionyso is also a respected throat singer and has a degree in ethnomusicology. The band has added Aaron's brother Benjamin to the mix, taking over the horn and woodwind work."},"works":[{"id":190314886046009,"type":"album","name":"Songbook Vol 1","artist":"Old Time Relijun","year":1997,"weight":6,"yt":"MGmWSvdQGO8","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":148308934912243,"type":"album","name":"Songbook Vol. I","artist":"Old Time Relijun","year":1997,"weight":3,"yt":"MGmWSvdQGO8","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":142489294796000,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Punk Blues","rank":160,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":58907275464000,"type":"album","name":"Utereus And Fire","artist":"Old Time Relijun","year":1999,"weight":6,"yt":"hChG3XjtCqs","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":241812413060755,"type":"album","name":"Uterus And Fire","artist":"Old Time Relijun","year":1999,"weight":6,"yt":"hChG3XjtCqs","src":"